  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$2 x^{2}+y^{2}+2 x y+2 x-3 y+8$\r\n$=\\frac{1}{2}\\left|4 x^{2}+2 y^{2}+4 x y+4 x-6 y+16\\right|$\r\n$=\\frac{1}{2}\\left[\\left(y^{2}-8 y\\right)+\\left(4 x^{2}+y^{2}+4 x y+4 x+2 y\\right)+16\\right].$\r\n$=\\frac{1}{2}\\left|(y-4)^{2}+(2 x+y+1)^{2}-1\\right|$\r\nSo, least value will be $-\\frac{1}{2}$ at $y=4$ and $x=\\frac{-5}{2}$",
    "image": null
  },
